From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:59:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/49] A3: check's extra worker takes packs only where it has
 a slot of its own

Port of the cost-map-10 test prototype p-ckx, with the condition tied
to the mechanism instead of a connection count. ReadPacks runs one
worker beside the configured ones. It reads through the backend's
additional load slot, which only the local backend at its default
connection count grants. On every other backend (REST, S3, SFTP, a
local repository with an explicit -o local.connections=N) its loads
joined the ordinary semaphore: one more check worker than the backend
has connections. There it now takes nothing, and check runs with the
configured number of workers, as stock does.

New: internal/repository/checker_extra_slot.go and its test. The test
fails without the condition (1, 2, 5 connections: 2, 3, 6 packs read at
the same time) and passes with it; with the slot granted the extra
worker still runs (3 at a time with 2 connections).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
